  "details": "1. Place a VRC Scale Constraint on the hand bone\n\n2. Set the source transform to some game object\n\n3. Animate that game object to scale down to 0\n\n4. Enter VR and enable the toggle to scale down the hand\n\nExpected result: Hand will shrink down to a point.\n\nActual result: Hand remains unaffected in-game.\n\nThe expected result was true until quite recently. This is also not an issue for any other bone except the hands or children of the hands.\n\nThis bug breaks scenarios where the hands need to be scaled or moved precisely with the use of constraints, where the scaling is important to prevent clipping or to suppress movement in the fingers.\n\nSetting the finger tracking to \"Animated\" does not work around this issue.\n\nThis issue does not appear on desktop mode. (To me, this suggests the issue comes from the vr hand tracking solutions, although it is weird that it is not helped by setting the tracking mode to \"animated\")",
